  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following is not an example of heterogeneous catalysis reaction?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Combustion of Coal",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Hydrogenation of Vegetable oils",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Ostwald's process",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Haber's process",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> Since Combustion of Coal is a fast and spontaneous process, no catalyst is required.<br /><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> Catalyst used in&nbsp;Hydrogenation of Vegetable oils is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ni</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> Catalyst used in&nbsp;Haber&#39;s process is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.<br /><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> Catalyst used in Ostwald&#39;s process is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Pt</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></math>"
  }
